    description: "## Origin\n\nFiled per hg-uat-v4.1.0 Round 07 incidental finding (master report §3 BUG-05). Independent of WI-pogus (which is the transitive-walk fix that's untestable on containerd until BUG-05 is closed). NOT parented to WI-pogus.\n\n## Symptom\n\ngrpc-linker-v1 emits implements_rpc edges where Go service-method overrides land on RPC routes from unrelated services. Affects 7 service families in containerd: Containers, Tasks, Namespaces, Images, Snapshots, Mounts, Content, Diff. All 7 collapse onto Leases/* RPCs. Zero implements_rpc edges land on those services' RPC routes despite each having a struct embedding the corresponding api.UnimplementedXxxServer.\n\n## Repro\n\n```bash\nhypergumbo run ~/ALL_REPOS/whole_bunch_of_repos/containerd --no-progress --out /tmp/r7.json\nzcat /tmp/r7.json.gz | jq '.edges[] | select(.origin==\"grpc-linker-v1\" and .type==\"implements_rpc\") | {src, dst}'\n```\n\nObserve that plugins/services/containers/service.go::service.Create resolves to RPC /containerd.services.leases.v1.Leases/Create, despite the local service struct embedding api.UnimplementedContainersServer.\n\n## Mechanism (sharpened per Round 08 §8.3)\n\nThe embedded Unimplemented*Server signal IS consulted on some code path — proven by controllerService.Update correctly resolving to Controller/Update through a 10-way method-name collision (Containers, Content, Controller, Images, Mounts, Namespaces, Snapshots, Store, Task, Tasks). 12 of 13 sampled cross-family disambiguations on controllerService and sandboxService land on the right service. Short-name match alone could not produce that pass rate.\n\nThe bug is therefore a **name-precondition gate** that diverts struct named 'service' (lowercase, no Service/Server suffix) to a short-name-fallback path before the embedded-signal-aware code runs. Plausible specific: the linker likely matches struct names against a regex like \\\\w+(Service|Server)$ to recognize gRPC server types. controllerService and sandboxService end in 'Service' (capital S); 'server' is the literal token. 'service' (lowercase) fails the precondition.\n\n## Scale\n\n- 7 service families affected in containerd; ~24 of 41 implements_rpc edges misresolved.\n- 0 implements_rpc edges land on Containers/Tasks/Snapshots/Mounts/Namespaces/Images/Content/Diff RPCs.\n- Conventional Go gRPC server name is 'service' (used by every containerd plugin) — high real-world incidence.\n\n## Severity rationale (HIGH)\n\nAny consumer of hypergumbo using implements_rpc to find which struct implements a given RPC (e.g., an LLM agent answering 'where is containerd.services.containers.v1.Containers/Create implemented?') will be sent to plugins/services/leases/service.go instead of plugins/services/containers/service.go. Wrong answer at the headline use case for the relation.\n\n## Fix scope (likely 1-2 lines)\n\nRemove or expand the name-precondition gate so that struct named 'service' enters the embedded-signal-aware path. Recognize the literal 'service' (and probably any struct that embeds an Unimplemented*Server, regardless of name).\n\n## Pre-fix fixture\n\nA Go file containing a struct literally named 'service' that embeds api.UnimplementedContainersServer (no other recognizable suffix). Methods on that struct should emit implements_rpc edges landing on Containers/* RPCs, not Leases/*.\n\n## Acceptance\n\n- Property test: a Go struct named 'service' embedding api.UnimplementedContainersServer emits implements_rpc edges to the Containers RPC family.\n- Regression guard: existing controllerService/sandboxService/server cases continue to resolve correctly.\n- Re-run on containerd: the 7 affected service families now emit non-zero implements_rpc edges to their canonical RPCs.\n\n## Carry-forward\n\nBUG-05 blocks honest assessment of WI-pogus's transitive walk on any Go target until the direct-embedding tier's correctness is restored. A re-route to kata-containers (per Round 07 plan caveat for WI-pogus) should follow a fix to BUG-05.\n\n## DQ-4 sub-case\n\nTTRPC-only services (no Unimplemented*Server at all) receive misleading Leases/* implements_rpc edges via the same short-name fallback. Recorded as DQ-4 in master report §4 because the right behavior for TTRPC may be 'emit nothing' or 'emit a TTRPC-flavored route' — design question beyond this fix's scope. Fold into BUG-05's fix decision rather than file separately.\n\n## References\n\n- Round 07 report: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-07-WI-pogus-go-grpc-ttrpc-transitive/report.md\n- Round 08 §8.3: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/round-08-followup-discriminators/report.md\n- Master report §3 BUG-05: ~/hypergumbo_lab_notebook/bakeoff_artifacts/hg-uat-v4.1.0/lab-notebook/master-report.md\n- Likely producer: packages/hypergumbo-core/src/hypergumbo_core/linkers/grpc.py"  # 329a
